 "note": "THE MODULE MAP (Phase 161h1, 7 Nov 2026; 09-app/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). Every file under src/: its area and its kind (page, logic, data, routes, other). doors: the one file of each area another area may import; until it exists, every import into the area is a break of rule 1. Read by tools/boundaries.cjs. A new file is placed here on purpose; moving a file to another area is a change to review.",
 "order_note": "THE ORDER (Phase 161l, 9 Nov 2026; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md rule 2): the areas from the bottom up. An area imports only areas below it; when a lower area must tell a higher one something, it announces an event (src/core/events.ts) or offers a port the higher one fills at start. clients (Phase 161l1) is the client record, low in the order so the modules can read a client without importing the CRM's screens above them. shared is at the bottom (plain tools: no sign-in, no SQL), then the core; app is the start-up wiring at the top, which nothing imports.",
